{
  "C2070-994__681dc6d83134c9f8": {
    "Question #: 1": {
      "Title": "Exam C2070-994 topic 1 question 20 discussion - ExamTopics",
      "Question": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "A company has determined through testing that they could improve Rulerunner performance for APT by adding additional threads to Rulerunner. Currently they have a Rulerunner server with 4 cores and 4 threads defined."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "How many more threads are recommended to add to the existing Rulerunner server?"
          }
        ]
      },
      "Choices": {
        "A": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "A. 0"
            }
          ]
        },
        "B": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "B. 2"
            }
          ]
        },
        "C": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "C. 4"
            }
          ]
        },
        "D": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "D. 8"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "Answer": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Suggested Answer: A \ud83d\uddf3\ufe0f"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "In general, you want the number of threads to match the number of processors in the host computer. For example, when Rulerunner is installed on a quad core server, enable four Rulerunner threads."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "References: https://www.ibm.com/support/knowledgecenter/en/SSZRWV_9.0.0/com.ibm.dc.install.doc/dcapt030.htm"
          }
        ]
      },
      "Explanation": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "In general, you want the number of threads to match the number of processors in the host computer. For example, when Rulerunner is installed on a quad core server, enable four Rulerunner threads."
